<title>SWEDEN: INSTANT VIEW -  Swedish Jan CPI +0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>INSTANT VIEW -  Swedish Jan CPI +0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's January consumer price index rose 0.1 percent for a year-on-year fall of 0.1 percent. The market had expected a rise of 0.4 percent for the month. In December, CPI fell 0.2 percent.</p>
<p>IAN GANNA, ECONOMIST AT CHASE</p>
<p>&quot;It was a pretty good figure. But I think the Riksbank needs more crown stability before they continue to cut the repo rate. The trend is probably changing now from deflation to rising prices.&quot;</p>
</text>
